<h2>What an implant-supported denture is</h2>
<p>An implant-supported denture (often called an overdenture or a snap-on denture) is a removable denture that locks securely onto two or more dental implants. Rather than relying on suction and adhesive to stay in place, it clips firmly onto attachments on the implants — so it doesn't move while you eat or talk.</p>

<h2>Who benefits most</h2>
<p>Patients who already wear a traditional denture and are frustrated with how it moves, slips, or causes sore spots are typically the happiest with the switch. It's also a good choice for patients who want a meaningful upgrade from a regular denture without the cost of a fully fixed full-arch reconstruction.</p>

<h2>Snap-on vs. fixed: how to decide</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>Snap-on (implant-supported):</strong> Removable for cleaning. Fewer implants. Lower cost. Still requires some palate coverage on the upper.</li>
  <li><strong>Fixed (All-on-4 / All-on-X):</strong> Never removed by you. Feels closest to natural teeth. Full bite force. Higher investment.</li>
</ul>
<p>At your consultation Dr. Phillips will lay out both options clearly, including the trade-offs and costs, and help you pick the right fit for your goals.</p>

<p>If you're comparing fixed and removable options, our blog guide can help you prepare: <a href="/blog/all-on-4-candidacy/">Am I a candidate for All-on-4?</a>.</p>
